---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import {getBrandCharts} from "../lib/content/brand-charts";
const charts=getBrandCharts();
---
<BaseLayout title="Goalie Pad Sizing Calculator & Brand Charts | Goalie Gear Fit" description="Find your goalie leg-pad size using reviewed Bauer, CCM, TRUE, Warrior and Brian's charts, then verify the fit at the knee block." dateModified="2026-08-21">
  <section class="fit-intro">
    <div class="fit-intro__copy"><p class="kicker">Independent pad sizing reference</p><h1>Find your goalie pad size by brand</h1><p class="fit-intro__lede">Start with the measurement your manufacturer actually uses. We match it to the published chart and tell you when the evidence is not enough.</p><p class="fit-intro__note"><strong>The result is a starting size.</strong> Your knee landing on the block is the final check.</p></div>
    <form class="fit-start" action="/calculator/" method="get"><div class="measure-scale" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:13},(_,i)=><span>{i%2===0?i+12:""}</span>)}</div><p class="fit-start__label">Sizing worksheet</p><h2>What is on your pads?</h2><label for="home-brand">Manufacturer</label><select id="home-brand" name="brand"><option value="bauer">Bauer</option><option value="ccm">CCM</option><option value="true">TRUE</option><option value="warrior">Warrior</option><option value="brians">Brian's</option></select><button class="button" type="submit">Start with this brand <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><a href="/guides/how-to-measure-goalie-pads/">I need to measure first</a></form>
  </section>
  <section class="brand-register" aria-labelledby="brand-heading"><header><p class="kicker">Chart register</p><h2 id="brand-heading">Reviewed manufacturer charts</h2><p>Brands do not use one universal sizing system. Each entry below keeps its own measurement method and category boundaries.</p></header><div class="brand-list">{charts.map(chart=><a class="brand-row" href={`/charts/${chart.slug}/`}><img class:list={["brand-row__logo",{"brand-logo--inverse":chart.vendor.inverseLogo}]} src={chart.vendor.logoPath} alt="" width="140" height="48" loading="lazy"/><span><strong>{chart.brand}</strong><small>{chart.rules.length} rules · {chart.categories.length} chart section{chart.categories.length===1?"":"s"}</small></span><span class="brand-row__method">Open chart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>)}</div></section>
  <section class="fit-process" aria-labelledby="process-heading"><header><p class="kicker">Use in this order</p><h2 id="process-heading">Measure, match, then put the pads on</h2></header><ol><li><span>1</span><div><strong>Use the right measuring line</strong><p>Floor-to-knee and ankle-to-knee are different inputs. Follow the instruction for your brand.</p></div></li><li><span>2</span><div><strong>Read the actual chart range</strong><p>Overlaps return adjacent options. A gap remains a gap; we do not round to the nearest size.</p></div></li><li><span>3</span><div><strong>Check the landing in your gear</strong><p>Wear skates and knee protection, drop into butterfly, and confirm your knee stays securely on the block.</p></div></li></ol></section>
  <aside class="evidence-note"><p class="kicker">A deliberate limitation</p><h2>Sometimes there is no responsible answer.</h2><div><p>The charts come from reviewed manufacturer guidance. We do not convert between unrelated measurement methods or fill missing rows with a guessed size.</p><p>Use every chart result as a starting point, then verify knee-block landing and overall pad movement in your full setup.</p><p><a href="/methodology/">How recommendations are reviewed</a> · <a href="/guides/thigh-rise-and-fit-check/">Physical fit check</a></p></div></aside>
</BaseLayout>
